'''''Helleborus argutifolius''''', the '''holly-leaved hellebore''', or '''Corsican hellebore''', [[synonym (taxonomy)|syn.]] ''H. corsicus'', ''H. lividus'' subsp. ''corsicus'' is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] Ranunculaceae, [[native plant|native]] to [[Corsica]] and [[Sardinia]], growing on hillsides, ravines, woodlands and roadsides.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Helleborus argutifolius - Plant Finder |url=https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=248767&isprofile=0&gen=Helleborus |access-date=2026-06-22 |website=www.missouribotanicalgarden.org}}</ref> It is an [[evergreen]] [[perennial plant|perennial]] growing to {{convert|120|cm|0|abbr=on}} tall by {{convert|90|cm|ft|0|abbr=on}} wide, with large leathery leaves comprising three spiny-toothed leaflets, and green bowl-shaped flowers in late winter and early spring.<ref name=RHSAZ>{{cite book|title=RHS A-Z encyclopedia of garden plants|year=2008|publisher=Dorling Kindersley|location=United Kingdom|isbn=978-1405332965|pages=1136}}</ref>

The Latin [[binomial nomenclature|specific epithet]] ''argutifolius'' means “with sharp-toothed leaves”.<ref name=RHSLG>{{cite book |last=Harrison |first=Lorraine |title=RHS Latin for Gardeners |year=2012 |publisher=Mitchell Beazley |location=United Kingdom |isbn=978-1845337315 }}</ref> 

In cultivation ''Helleborus argutifolius'' [[Hybrid (biology)#Hybrid plants|hybridises]] readily with the closely related ''[[Helleborus lividus|H. lividus]]''.<ref>{{cite web|title=Helleborus argutifolius, Viviani (1824)|url=http://www.hellebores.org/argutifolius.html|publisher=hellebores.org|access-date=23 December 2012}}</ref> ''H. argutifolius'' has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web|title=''Helleborus argutifolius'' AGM|url= https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/8565/Helleborus-argutifolius/Details |publisher=Royal Horticultural Society|access-date=6 August 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web  | url= https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/agm-lists/agm-ornamentals.pdf | title = AGM Plants - Ornamental | date = July 2017 | page = 47 | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | access-date = 3 March 2018}}</ref> 

